WEBVTT

00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:03.850
Let's go!

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:04.620
We can do it!

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:06.020
Wake Up, Girls!

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:32.650
Green Leaves Entertainment

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:33.450
Let's give it all we have, 
Wake Up, Girls!

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:39.980
Huh?

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:42.770
It's not that easy...

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:44.680
We can't shift gears that quickly.

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:45.540
What?

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:50.900
You and Sudo-san 
both treated us poorly.

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:53.800
Shut up! 
There's nothing wrong with me.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.800
You're in for a surprise this time.

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:00.250
This really is a huge surprise!

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:02.680
<b>Variety Show Proposal 
Local Gourmet "Absolutely Delicious" 
Scalding Weather Report "It's Really Hot"</b>

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:01.050
Listen up, girls.

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:05.800
You're going to be doing a three-minute corner on a variety program.

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:06.950
You'll split into two groups.

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:09.050
The gourmet report will be 
Mondays, Wednesdays, and Fridays.

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:12.990
The scalding weather report will be
Tuesdays, Thursdays, and Saturdays.

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:13.570
Question.

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:14.580
What?

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:17.590
What exactly is a "scalding" 
weather report?

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:20.480
I can't believe you're asking that.

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:21.200
What?

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.350
You're not new to this business.

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:28.080
There's something you need 
to know before I explain.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:35.340
<b>Pie Throwing 
Bald Wigs 
Scalding Water</b>

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:32.690
In the beginning, 
idols just needed to be cute.

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:35.340
That only lasted until the mid '70s.

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:40.420
Since then, in order to survive, 
idols have taken pies in the face,

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:45.880
worn bald wigs, and thrown 
themselves into scalding water.

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:47.980
So, what?

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:50.570
Have you even been listening?!

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:53.600
In other words, only those 
who undergo these trials

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:55.730
will become true idols.

00:02:57.270 --> 00:02:59.770
Giving a weather report 
in scalding water

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:02.590
is an appealing proposal for idols.

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:04.810
Who wouldn't want to do it?

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:08.410
<b>Local Gourmet "Super Delicious" 
Scalding Weather Report "It's Really Hot"</b>

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:11.380
This plan was unsolicited, 
wasn't it?

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:15.300
Your thinking is 
a little ridiculous.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:16.920
Are you trying to trip us up?

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:18.730
We'll decide who's doing what.

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:19.200
Are you listening?

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:20.670
Who wants to do the gourmet show?

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:22.430
Who wants to do the scalding water?

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:24.800
Are you stupid?

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:28.980
Of course no one wants 
to sit in scalding water.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:30.060
Yeah.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:32.000
Fine, then.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:32.980
We'll draw straws.

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:34.730
Straws?

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:36.980
I hope I get what I want.

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:41.210
You girls are the scalding water group,

00:03:41.210 --> 00:03:43.160
and you girls are the gourmet group.

00:03:43.630 --> 00:03:45.810
Let's start rehearsing.

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:47.910
Don't push me.

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:50.910
You'd better not push me.

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:54.010
Hot!

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:55.350
It's so hot!

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.000
Ice, ice.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.180
It's so hot.

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:04.020
Sorry. When you told us not 
to push you, I couldn't help myself.

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:04.890
Are you okay?

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:07.670
This isn't possible.

00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:09.740
What? Don't complain to me.

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:13.630
Isn't a manager's job 
protecting his clients?

00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:14.890
Good grief.

00:04:16.490 --> 00:04:18.650
Man, you girls sure got lucky.

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:24.650
You're not hot anymore, right?

00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:27.790
I'm not hot, 
but my head is so heavy...

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:30.350
An animal weather report 
is a great idea.

00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:33.160
It's refreshing.

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:39.340
This is so good!

00:04:40.870 --> 00:04:42.010
So good!

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:48.140
Cream yakisoba bread is so good!

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:52.220
Mind if I have these?

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:53.550
Go ahead.

00:04:53.550 --> 00:04:55.240
Thanks for the food!

00:04:56.410 --> 00:04:58.150
It's so good!

00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:01.110
You sure are a big eater.

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:04.090
As long as we have you, 
I don't need to worry about this group.

00:05:04.090 --> 00:05:05.510
Thank you.

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:07.090
Keep up the good work, girls.

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:09.850
Make sure you memorize the script.

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:11.730
Okay, we will.

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:18.810
Huh? We don't have any lines.

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:21.540
We probably have to ad lib.

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:23.120
Ad lib?

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:25.670
We can say whatever we want.

00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:28.380
Yeah, but...

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:34.430
Animal idol, Hayashida Airi, 
will bring you tomorrow's weather, as well.

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:37.310
First, Miyagi-ken...

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:38.520
She stuttered.

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:39.940
Look at the camera.

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:41.390
Um...

00:05:41.390 --> 00:05:43.650
What? What's going on?

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:43.300
Hey!

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:44.390
Calm down!

00:05:44.390 --> 00:05:47.620
They're experiencing 
a different kind of freedom.

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:48.700
Yeah.

00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:52.790
Our first episode is seafood specialties.

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:55.120
I wonder what we'll get to eat.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:56.790
Hello!

00:05:55.120 --> 00:06:02.880
<b>Local Gourmet 
Super Delicious</b>

00:05:55.120 --> 00:06:02.880
<b>Broadcast</b>

00:05:55.120 --> 00:06:02.880
<b>First Appearance!</b>

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:58.280
Hello!

00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:02.880
We're members of the Sendai-based 
group, Wake Up, Girls!

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:04.880
Thanks for watching!

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:07.280
You're so stiff.

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:09.700
Relax your shoulders.

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:12.370
It's raining really hard, though.

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:14.010
<b>Welcome to the Marine Park</b>

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:14.010
Speak Loudly

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:14.010
I guess they can't help it.

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:20.230
Uh, um...

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:22.820
Come on. Say something.

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:25.320
What is this? It's so gross.

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:27.070
Nanami, no!

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:29.070
Comment!

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:30.570
This isn't good.

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:36.080
It's so good!

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:38.080
Comment!

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:41.170
Ascidians are an 
Ishinomaki specialty.

00:06:41.170 --> 00:06:45.090
As someone originally from 
Ishinomaki, I love them.

00:06:50.030 --> 00:06:51.490
Amazing! Amazing!

00:06:51.490 --> 00:06:53.070
That was really great.

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:54.550
Thank you.

00:06:54.550 --> 00:06:57.290
You're especially great.

00:06:57.290 --> 00:06:58.870
Thank you.

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:00.020
Is there anything you don't like?

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:00.790
Nope.

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:02.180
It's just, you know...

00:07:02.180 --> 00:07:02.810
What?

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:04.660
Instead of just saying 
everything's good,

00:07:04.660 --> 00:07:09.320
it'd be better if you 
expanded your vocabulary.

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:11.820
I understand.

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:14.230
Well, see you next time.

00:07:14.230 --> 00:07:14.910
Yes.

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:17.020
We look forward to working with you.

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:21.280
I was worried for a minute there, 
but Minami, nice work.

00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:21.810
Huh?

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:23.410
Minami, thanks.

00:07:23.410 --> 00:07:26.890
What? I really did 
think it was good...

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:30.110
What's wrong?

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:34.220
The director told me just 
saying good isn't good enough.

00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:52.610
<b>Local Gourmet 
Super Delicious</b>

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:52.610
<b>Broadcast</b>

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:52.610
<b>Today's Specialty is 
Something Really Delicious</b>

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:38.510
Hello, everyone.

00:07:38.510 --> 00:07:40.590
We are Wake Up, Girls!

00:07:40.590 --> 00:07:43.520
Today, we're at a Sendai 
beef tongue restaurant.

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:46.600
At this restaurant, 
if you finish one kilogram

00:07:46.600 --> 00:07:48.370
of beef tongue in 
thirty minutes, it's free.

00:07:48.370 --> 00:07:51.100
We'd like to accept that challenge.

00:07:51.100 --> 00:07:52.610
Thanks for the food!

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:09.170
<b>Local Gourmet 
Super Delicious</b>

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:09.170
<b>Broadcast</b>

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:09.170
<b>Today's Specialty is 
Beef Tongue!!</b>

00:07:58.760 --> 00:08:00.730
This is a lot of food.

00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:02.290
Yeah.

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:04.380
Minami, can you still eat more?

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:05.650
Huh? Yeah.

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:08.460
After all, it's goo— I mean, um...

00:08:12.370 --> 00:08:14.510
Um...

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:16.290
What's wrong, Minami?

00:08:16.290 --> 00:08:18.010
Saying it's good is fine.

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:22.020
<b>Local Gourmet 
Super Delicious</b>

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:22.020
<b>Broadcast</b>

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:22.020
<b>Today's Specialty is 
Beef Tongue!!</b>

00:08:20.440 --> 00:08:22.020
It's really tasty, meow!

00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:26.540
<b>Broadcast</b>

00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:26.540
<b>Today's Specialty is 
Fried Gourd</b>

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:26.540
<b>Local Gourmet 
Super Delicious</b>

00:08:25.390 --> 00:08:27.020
It's really tasty, meow!

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:29.290
<b>Local Gourmet 
Super Delicious</b>

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:29.290
<b>Broadcast</b>

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:29.290
<b>Today's Specialty is 
Hazekura Sweets</b>

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:29.720
It's really tasty, meow!

00:08:29.290 --> 00:08:32.030
<b>Local Gourmet 
Super Delicious</b>

00:08:29.290 --> 00:08:32.030
<b>Broadcast</b>

00:08:29.290 --> 00:08:32.030
<b>Today's Specialty is 
Taikichi Taiyaki!!</b>

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:32.030
It's really tasty, meow!

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:33.850
Amazing, amazing!

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:44.040
<b>Sakura Cream 100 yen
You Can Do It, Sendai!</b>

00:08:33.850 --> 00:08:34.900
You're super amazing!

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:39.300
This corner's rating 
is skyrocketing.

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:40.760
Let's keep up the good work.

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:42.350
Let's keep eating.

00:08:42.350 --> 00:08:43.510
E-Excuse me...

00:08:43.510 --> 00:08:44.040
Huh?

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:46.510
Oh, "it's really tasty, meow!"

00:08:46.510 --> 00:08:47.790
That's great.

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:49.340
Really?

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:50.800
Why would I lie?

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:52.120
Good job.

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:53.340
That's great.

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:54.190
Yeah.

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:56.930
Animal Weather Report!

00:08:54.800 --> 00:09:27.170
<b>Animal 
Weather Report</b>

00:08:54.800 --> 00:09:27.170
<b>Tomorrow's 
Weather</b>

00:08:57.770 --> 00:09:00.090
Miyagi's weather tomorrow is rain.

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:02.560
There's a 100% chance of rain.

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:04.570
Rain is so depressing.

00:09:04.570 --> 00:09:06.940
I went to the zoo the other day.

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:10.070
A lot of animals don't seem 
to like the rain, either.

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:11.410
That's right.

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:14.240
The lesser pandas came outside,

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:17.690
but they looked bored 
staring at the sky.

00:09:17.690 --> 00:09:20.960
Did you know lesser pandas 
are also known as red pandas?

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:24.160
Whenever I hear it, I think there 
might be other colors of pandas.

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:25.570
I don't.

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:29.210
<b>Yakitori</b>

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:29.210
<b>Senichiya</b>

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:29.210
That's great news.

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:33.090
The gourmet show and weather report 
both received good reviews.

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:34.190
Yeah.

00:09:34.190 --> 00:09:38.260
I wasn't sure about it at first, 
but everyone's getting used to it.

00:09:38.260 --> 00:09:39.240
There, there.

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:42.350
Minami's gourmet report 
is especially popular.

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:43.840
You're right.

00:09:43.840 --> 00:09:47.580
I always thought Minami 
was a strong eater.

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:51.820
And that's exactly why I scouted her.

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:54.090
What? I thought you saw 
her singing a folk song

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:56.490
and scouted her for her voice.

00:09:56.490 --> 00:09:57.670
There's that, too.

00:09:57.670 --> 00:09:58.560
No way.

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:00.620
You just made that up.

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:02.490
You're always making things up.

00:10:02.490 --> 00:10:04.330
Don't worry about the details.

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:05.160
There it is again.

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:06.370
Either way...

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:13.210
<b>Staying Connected</b>

00:10:07.520 --> 00:10:10.820
She was like an idol to the 
folk song club that was formed

00:10:10.820 --> 00:10:16.590
by the people who live in the 
Ishinomaki temporary homes.

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:20.090
She was shining.

00:10:21.370 --> 00:10:23.570
She smelled like money.

00:10:23.570 --> 00:10:24.470
Is that your reason?

00:10:25.310 --> 00:10:26.790
Anyway... What did you 
want to talk about?

00:10:26.790 --> 00:10:27.900
Oh, right.

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:31.050
In reward for their improving ratings,

00:10:31.050 --> 00:10:36.180
they're doing a concert at the 
Sendai TV Thanksgiving Festival.

00:10:36.180 --> 00:10:38.250
Really? That's great, Matsuda!

00:10:38.250 --> 00:10:39.030
Yeah...

00:10:39.690 --> 00:10:42.770
That's it! One step at a time!

00:10:42.770 --> 00:10:44.800
One step in one day, 
three steps in three...

00:10:44.800 --> 00:10:47.000
Three steps forward 
and four steps back!

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:48.230
That's how it goes.

00:10:48.230 --> 00:10:50.500
Huh? That doesn't move you forward.

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:53.700
Thanks for the food!

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:58.280
<b>Local Gourmet 
Super Delicious</b>

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:58.280
<b>Broadcast</b>

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:58.280
<b>Today's Specialty is 
Really Good Pancakes!!</b>

00:10:56.650 --> 00:10:58.620
It's really tasty, meow!

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:01.260
That's just like Minami-chan.

00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:04.790
She really looks like 
she's enjoying her food.

00:11:04.790 --> 00:11:06.870
This job is perfect for her.

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:08.680
It really is.

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:13.080
Seeing Minami-chan 
makes us want to eat, too.

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:14.030
You're right.

00:11:14.030 --> 00:11:14.860
You're drooling.

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:17.440
It's because of Minami-chan.

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:24.450
Today, we have a message 
for our viewers.

00:11:24.900 --> 00:11:31.220
As you know, we're the Sendai-based 
idol group, Wake Up, Girls!

00:11:31.220 --> 00:11:33.450
We have a total of seven members,

00:11:33.450 --> 00:11:38.110
including the three of us and 
the four on the animal weather report.

00:11:38.110 --> 00:11:43.290
On the special stage of this Sunday's 
Sendai TV Thanksgiving Festival,

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:46.350
<b>Sendai TV </b>Thanksgiving 2014

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:46.350
<b>Concert Opens!</b>

00:11:43.290 --> 00:11:46.350
we'll be performing a concert.

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:49.700
It's a heart-pounding and 
exciting live performance.

00:11:49.700 --> 00:11:53.540
If you live in the area, 
come check us out.

00:11:53.540 --> 00:11:55.360
We hope to see you there!

00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:55.360
Why don't we go?

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:56.570
What?

00:11:56.570 --> 00:11:59.970
Let's go to Sendai 
together next Sunday.

00:11:59.970 --> 00:12:02.280
Yes, let's go.

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:04.270
Let's all crash the concert.

00:12:04.270 --> 00:12:05.350
That's a great idea.

00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:07.260
Should we make something?

00:12:07.260 --> 00:12:08.030
Like lunches?

00:12:08.030 --> 00:12:09.120
No, not that.

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:10.970
They're idols.

00:12:10.970 --> 00:12:17.430
Young people have those fans, 
coats, and glowing things.

00:12:17.430 --> 00:12:19.210
Oh, right.

00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:20.380
Let's make those.

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:23.120
There are all kinds 
of colors these days.

00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:25.270
What color does Minami-chan prefer?

00:12:25.270 --> 00:12:26.140
Do you know?

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:28.260
I wonder.

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:30.430
Thank you!

00:12:30.430 --> 00:12:32.570
We got to eat good food again today!

00:12:32.570 --> 00:12:37.340
I think your smile 
inspired me to eat a lot.

00:12:37.340 --> 00:12:39.900
My stomach has been getting bigger.

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:41.010
Really?

00:12:41.010 --> 00:12:41.860
Yeah.

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:44.470
I'm excited for our next shoot.

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:44.760
Protective Charm

00:12:46.360 --> 00:12:47.320
Minami.

00:12:50.010 --> 00:12:50.910
Thanks.

00:12:51.550 --> 00:12:53.940
It would have been 
terrible if I lost this.

00:12:53.940 --> 00:12:55.040
Is that your protective charm?

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:55.870
Yeah.

00:12:56.580 --> 00:13:00.250
Grandma Isokawa in my folk song club

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:04.950
made it for me when 
I auditioned for Wake Up, Girls!

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:09.010
I have stage fright, so this would 
protect me from making mistakes.

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:11.260
You have stage fright?

00:13:11.260 --> 00:13:14.890
Yeah. I get nervous so easily.

00:13:14.890 --> 00:13:16.870
You don't seem that way.

00:13:17.530 --> 00:13:20.270
That must be because of this charm.

00:13:20.710 --> 00:13:22.440
When I passed the audition,

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:26.790
Grandma Isokawa celebrated 
like she was the one who got in.

00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:29.120
Yay!

00:13:30.100 --> 00:13:33.330
They've been supporting 
me ever since then.

00:13:33.940 --> 00:13:35.430
I see.

00:13:35.430 --> 00:13:39.770
They even watch our 
gourmet corner every day.

00:13:39.770 --> 00:13:40.500
Really.

00:13:40.930 --> 00:13:43.370
I'm going to invite 
them to our concert.

00:13:43.370 --> 00:13:46.370
Actually, since they 
saw today's broadcast,

00:13:46.370 --> 00:13:49.970
I'm sure they'll say they're 
going when I get home.

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:54.640
I'm home.

00:13:57.160 --> 00:13:58.190
Mayu-chan.

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:04.400
Mayu, isn't there something 
you want to tell me?

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:05.230
What?

00:14:06.050 --> 00:14:08.550
Why are you starting this again?

00:14:09.150 --> 00:14:10.160
I...

00:14:11.530 --> 00:14:14.290
How much more do you 
have to make me suffer?

00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:16.850
I'm not trying to do that.

00:14:16.850 --> 00:14:19.500
I just want to try again.

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:22.060
Wait!

00:14:22.060 --> 00:14:24.810
Why don't you listen 
to what Mayu-chan has to say?

00:14:29.520 --> 00:14:33.140
By the way, Minami-chan, 
what's your color?

00:14:33.140 --> 00:14:34.850
What? Color?

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:39.420
Yeah, we forgot to ask.

00:14:39.420 --> 00:14:43.610
We just assumed it was yellow.

00:14:44.020 --> 00:14:46.550
They say big eaters are yellow.

00:14:46.550 --> 00:14:47.150
Huh?

00:14:47.150 --> 00:14:50.520
Minami-chan doesn't know 
what you're talking about.

00:14:50.520 --> 00:14:55.120
We haven't been assigned 
colors yet, but why yellow?

00:14:55.710 --> 00:14:58.620
Because you're like the sun.

00:14:58.620 --> 00:14:59.680
Huh?

00:14:59.680 --> 00:15:05.630
If we're flowers, you are 
the sun that illuminates us.

00:15:05.950 --> 00:15:06.850
Right?

00:15:06.850 --> 00:15:07.630
Yeah.

00:15:07.630 --> 00:15:08.560
Yes, that's right.

00:15:08.560 --> 00:15:09.470
You think so?

00:15:09.940 --> 00:15:10.910
Okay, then.

00:15:10.910 --> 00:15:12.380
Tada!

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:14.780
<b>You can do it, Minami-chan!</b>

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:22.150
Green Leaves Entertainment

00:15:17.480 --> 00:15:19.530
The concert is tomorrow.

00:15:19.530 --> 00:15:21.430
Matsuda, where's the set list?

00:15:21.430 --> 00:15:22.150
Here.

00:15:22.770 --> 00:15:25.970
They still only have one song.

00:15:25.970 --> 00:15:28.340
The rest are covers.

00:15:28.340 --> 00:15:32.140
Do you think we could ask 
Twinkle for another song?

00:15:32.140 --> 00:15:33.560
You're right.

00:15:33.560 --> 00:15:35.670
Have the costumes arrived?

00:15:35.670 --> 00:15:37.160
All seven have arrived.

00:15:37.570 --> 00:15:40.290
The costumes we've been 
waiting for are ready.

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:41.620
Let's get to it, girls.

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:42.390
Yes.

00:15:42.390 --> 00:15:44.570
Go rehearse your hearts out.

00:15:44.570 --> 00:15:47.170
It's a local show, 
but it's a live broadcast.

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:48.920
Let's show them what we've got!

00:15:48.920 --> 00:15:49.500
Yes!

00:15:49.500 --> 00:15:51.300
Let's bring back the head of Sendai!

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:52.180
The head?

00:15:52.670 --> 00:15:54.180
Come on! Show some spirit!

00:15:54.570 --> 00:15:57.040
Good work today.

00:15:57.040 --> 00:15:57.640
Bye.

00:15:58.000 --> 00:16:01.100
I'm excited to perform again.

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:03.940
Are the members 
of the folk song club coming?

00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:04.760
Yeah.

00:16:04.760 --> 00:16:08.000
They made a huge banner.

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:08.590
Really?

00:16:08.590 --> 00:16:13.090
The banner's a beautiful 
yellow color.

00:16:13.090 --> 00:16:13.910
Yellow, huh?

00:16:14.580 --> 00:16:17.700
They said I'm like the sun 
that illuminates them.

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:19.830
That's why it's yellow.

00:16:20.520 --> 00:16:23.250
Yeah, you just might be the sun.

00:16:25.560 --> 00:16:27.500
What? You're kidding.

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:30.090
She suddenly said 
her chest hurt last night.

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:32.110
We called an ambulance, 
and she went to the hospital.

00:16:32.110 --> 00:16:33.930
Is she okay?

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:37.190
Kisaragi-san will stay with her.

00:16:37.190 --> 00:16:41.690
On the way to the hospital, 
Isokawa-san asked us

00:16:41.690 --> 00:16:44.940
to wish you luck at your concert.

00:16:45.850 --> 00:16:46.440
I can't...

00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:47.740
What?

00:16:47.740 --> 00:16:53.110
I can't leave her to go to a concert 
when she's in the hospital.

00:16:53.110 --> 00:16:54.720
Minami-chan.

00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:56.500
I can't do it! Where is she?

00:16:56.500 --> 00:16:58.070
Which hospital is she at?

00:16:58.070 --> 00:16:59.330
Take me there!

00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:00.050
Minami-chan...

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:00.870
Take me there!

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:05.290
Is everyone here?

00:17:05.830 --> 00:17:07.670
Minami's still not here.

00:17:07.670 --> 00:17:08.220
What?

00:17:08.220 --> 00:17:10.760
Minami's never late.

00:17:10.760 --> 00:17:12.660
Maybe something happened.

00:17:12.660 --> 00:17:13.430
Yeah.

00:17:13.430 --> 00:17:14.630
She answered her phone.

00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:16.800
Minami? Where are you?

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:19.440
Are you girls ready?

00:17:19.440 --> 00:17:21.100
What? What's wrong?

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:22.890
It's Minami.

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:23.770
What?

00:17:24.470 --> 00:17:27.980
Grandma Isokawa is in the hospital...

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:28.980
Hold on.

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:30.930
I'm giving the phone 
to the president.

00:17:30.930 --> 00:17:32.040
It's Minami.

00:17:32.890 --> 00:17:35.240
Hello? What's going on?

00:17:36.690 --> 00:17:37.860
Yes.

00:17:38.440 --> 00:17:39.340
I see.

00:17:40.300 --> 00:17:42.620
So, you can't come here?

00:17:43.140 --> 00:17:45.820
Minami's friend is hospitalized.

00:17:45.820 --> 00:17:47.000
She can't come.

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:47.750
What?

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:49.050
What are we going to do?

00:17:49.050 --> 00:17:51.850
Don't ask me. I don't know.

00:17:56.890 --> 00:17:58.900
We'll perform without Minami.

00:17:58.900 --> 00:17:59.860
Without her?

00:17:59.860 --> 00:18:03.720
But you said we'd promote 
Minami in the concert.

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:06.020
I'll explain the situation 
to the TV station.

00:18:06.830 --> 00:18:10.370
Someone important 
to Minami is in the hospital.

00:18:10.370 --> 00:18:15.190
You should understand 
the desire to help her.

00:18:16.500 --> 00:18:18.200
We'll cover for her.

00:18:18.760 --> 00:18:20.550
Figure out the performance 
between the six of you.

00:18:20.550 --> 00:18:21.070
Okay.

00:18:21.070 --> 00:18:24.580
Matsuda, let's go see the producer.

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:25.110
Huh?

00:18:25.110 --> 00:18:27.550
You can never be too sorry.

00:18:27.550 --> 00:18:28.330
Okay.

00:18:40.530 --> 00:18:42.050
Grandma...

00:18:42.440 --> 00:18:45.060
Minami-chan, what are you doing here?

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:47.120
Because... because...

00:18:47.120 --> 00:18:48.520
You're in the hospital!

00:18:53.570 --> 00:18:55.150
Should you be taking that off?

00:18:55.150 --> 00:18:55.780
I'm fine.

00:18:55.780 --> 00:18:57.860
I don't need this.

00:19:02.820 --> 00:19:04.870
Will you make it 
in time for your concert?

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:06.090
I'm not going.

00:19:06.090 --> 00:19:07.370
I'm staying here.

00:19:07.990 --> 00:19:09.500
You have to go.

00:19:10.010 --> 00:19:11.170
But...

00:19:11.170 --> 00:19:12.310
No.

00:19:12.310 --> 00:19:17.500
If you came here for me, 
go to the concert instead.

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:26.710
The best medicine for me 
is to see you dancing.

00:19:28.140 --> 00:19:32.440
Didn't I tell you? 
You're like the sun.

00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:38.580
You illuminated us 
as we were wilting.

00:19:39.860 --> 00:19:45.950
You need to keep being 
the sun that illuminates us.

00:19:48.930 --> 00:19:50.100
Go on.

00:19:50.100 --> 00:19:51.960
I'll be fine.

00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:54.570
I've been through a lot.

00:19:54.570 --> 00:19:58.170
It'll take more than 
this to take me out.

00:19:58.170 --> 00:19:59.130
Okay?

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:10.930
Can we practice our positions 
for "Stand Up" again?

00:20:10.930 --> 00:20:13.810
We just did it.

00:20:13.810 --> 00:20:15.380
I'm sorry.

00:20:15.380 --> 00:20:17.690
Let's do it one more time.

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:25.050
It's almost time.

00:20:25.050 --> 00:20:25.860
Okay.

00:20:26.950 --> 00:20:28.830
Don't make that sound.

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:31.200
You're making me nervous.

00:20:32.540 --> 00:20:33.460
Minami.

00:20:33.890 --> 00:20:35.960
Is it okay for you to be here?

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:37.130
Yeah.

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:38.750
Sorry I'm late.

00:20:40.090 --> 00:20:41.750
I'm sorry.

00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:43.760
It's fine.

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:45.550
Are you sure you 
should be here, though?

00:20:45.550 --> 00:20:46.480
Yes.

00:20:46.480 --> 00:20:49.560
This will make 
Grandma Isokawa happier.

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:52.010
I see.

00:20:52.010 --> 00:20:52.980
You'd better hurry, then.

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:54.130
There's no time.

00:20:54.130 --> 00:20:54.880
Okay.

00:20:54.880 --> 00:20:56.760
Oh, Matsuda-san.

00:20:56.760 --> 00:20:57.680
What is it?

00:20:57.680 --> 00:20:58.690
I'd like to change.

00:20:58.690 --> 00:21:00.480
Could you take me 
to the waiting room?

00:21:00.480 --> 00:21:01.070
Roger that.

00:21:04.460 --> 00:21:05.450
<i>...without giving up</i>

00:21:05.450 --> 00:21:11.310
<i>WAKE UP bathed in bright sunlight</i>

00:21:11.790 --> 00:21:18.040
<i>The hope in my heart overlaps with you</i>

00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:15.540
<b>You can do it, Minami!</b>

00:21:18.040 --> 00:21:23.550
<i>STAND UP There is no night that does not end</i>

00:21:19.540 --> 00:21:21.550
<b>You can do it, Minami!</b>

00:21:23.550 --> 00:21:30.050
<i>Believe in tomorrow's smile</i>

00:21:23.550 --> 00:21:30.050
<b>You can do it, Minami!</b>

00:21:25.200 --> 00:21:30.050
Minami is a ray of hope that 
illuminates everything around her.

00:21:30.050 --> 00:21:32.310
<i>Shine</i>

00:21:30.050 --> 00:21:36.530
<i>Shine MY ONLY ONE</i>

00:21:32.700 --> 00:21:35.310
Isn't she great?

00:21:38.890 --> 00:21:40.620
Thank you very much.

00:21:40.620 --> 00:21:42.820
Thank you very much!

00:21:46.950 --> 00:21:48.570
Former I-1 Mayushi's Sendai idol WUG thread 
Entertainment Production Company "Green Leaves Entertainment" HP 

00:21:50.330 --> 00:21:52.830
Former I-1's Mayushi is back!! 
Sendai TV's concert was awesome! 
I'm glad I followed her...

00:21:54.010 --> 00:21:55.230
Mayushi?

00:21:55.230 --> 00:21:56.330
Shimada Mayu, huh?

00:21:56.330 --> 00:22:01.340
Yes. She's working with 
Sendai's Wake Up, Girls!

00:22:02.950 --> 00:22:05.880
The rumors were true.

00:22:08.380 --> 00:22:11.890
<b>Internal Conflict in I-1?</b>

00:22:08.380 --> 00:22:11.890
<b>Shimada Mayu retires?!</b>

00:22:08.380 --> 00:22:11.890
<b>Shimada Mayu leaves?!</b>

00:22:11.890 --> 00:22:14.930
To be continued

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:47.920
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:45.360 --> 00:23:48.050
Yoppi, you've been acting 
since you were little, right?

00:23:48.050 --> 00:23:50.290
Yeah, I've been doing 
it since I was four.

00:23:50.290 --> 00:23:51.370
What kind of roles 
have you performed?

00:23:51.370 --> 00:23:52.430
I've done all kinds of things.

00:23:52.430 --> 00:23:55.260
Oh, but I did one thing 
better than anyone else.

00:23:55.260 --> 00:23:56.010
Really? What was it?

00:23:56.010 --> 00:23:57.050
Corpses!

00:23:57.530 --> 00:24:00.000
The next episode is 
"Scandal!"

